course: dictionary
lesson: 5917
title: Animal words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a new word from the words around it. This is its context, and it leaves clues. «There are hundreds of kinds of monkeys, from a pygmy marmoset that could sit on your finger to a mandrill heavier than a big dog.» The size comparison tells you a marmoset is a very small animal.
explain: Clues can also come from what you already know about a place or an animal. Marmosets live in trees, eat fruit, insects and tree gum, and live in family groups. Those clues help you picture the animal before you look up a single fact.
explain: Check your guess by swapping it into the sentence. «Tamarins and marmosets usually have twins» still makes sense if you think of a marmoset as a small monkey. If your meaning fits every sentence, you are probably right.
fact: A marmoset is a very small monkey with a long tail, soft fur and often tufts of hair on its ears.
fact: Marmosets live in the rainforests of South America, where they live in trees.
fact: Marmosets eat fruit, insects and tree gum, and they live in family groups.
fact: «The pygmy marmoset from the Amazon is the smallest monkey, about 100 grams.»
fact: Animal charities say marmosets should not be kept as pets, because they need special care and company.
exercise: «The pygmy marmoset from the Amazon is the smallest monkey, about 100 grams.» What is a marmoset? | A kind of tree | *A very small monkey with a long tail | A large dog with a red face | A bird that sings in the rainforest
exercise: Maya reads «a family of marmosets» and asks what that means. Which answer is right? | A zoo where monkeys are sold | A single marmoset on its own | *A group of marmosets living together | A fruit tree with monkeys on it
exercise: Where do marmosets live in the wild? | In deserts in Africa | *In the rainforests of South America | In the snow on mountain tops | Under the sea
test: «Tamarins and marmosets usually have twins, and the father and older brothers and sisters carry the babies most of the time.» Who carries the babies most of the time? | The mother alone, all day and all night | The zookeepers | *The father and older brothers and sisters | The babies carry themselves
test: Animal charities say marmosets should not be kept as pets. Why? | They can talk like people | They are too big to fit in a house | *They need special care and company | They only eat stones
exam: «A pygmy marmoset that could sit on your finger» tells you a lot. What is a pygmy marmoset? | *A tiny monkey that could sit on your finger | A kind of tree with sweet fruit | A bird with bright feathers | A huge monkey heavier than a big dog
